      "writtenOn": "2023-11-29T17:34:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I read this section of the spec, but I\u0027m still confused about this value.\n\nIt looks like the procedure is specified in terms of the current security level, but I don\u0027t understand why a device would have a max security level.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 56,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 56,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "16c7aba9b698e8c7cc1f5cae812d27fdf4ac1f14",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d48cba3c_38a4eacc",
        "filename": "bluetooth/ranging/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/ranging/IBluetoothChannelSounding.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1322510
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-30T06:37:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Based on the spec, the application can select preferred security level for CS.\nThe max supported security level of CS is depends on capabilities of local/remote device which exchaged during setup phase.\n\nLevel 1 - All mandatory CS features\nLevel 2 - All mandatory CS features\nLevel 3 - All mandatory CS features, RTT_Capability\u003d0x7\nLevel 4 - All mandatory CS features, RTT_Capability\u003d0x7, Optional_NADM_Sounding_Capability\u003d0x1, Optional_NADM_Random_Capability\u003d0x1\n\nOn the other hand, I think the ranging algorithm should be able to handle the corresponding ranging data as well.\nFor example, if an APP enable CS with level 2, we will get ranging data that contains Tone and RTT.\nIf the ranging algorithm can only handle tone data but ignore RTT, we should not claim we support level 2.\nThis is why we need this API to check the max supported security level for ranging algorithms.\n\nThanks!",
      "parentUuid": "1657af35_2db42b51",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 56,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 56,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "16c7aba9b698e8c7cc1f5cae812d27fdf4ac1f14",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c718ac92_7f4fe7ef",
        "filename": "bluetooth/ranging/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/ranging/IBluetoothChannelSounding.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076123
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-01T00:14:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I were an app developer, I would want to set a required security level, and have the rest handled in the background.\n\nIf my application requires security level 2, any higher level should be fine.\n\nSetMinimumSecurityLevel()\n\nOr maybe have a minimum security level as part of StartSession?\n\nIt feels like SetMinimumSecurityLevel could have the same effect as GetMaximum, but it would be easier to use.",
      "parentUuid": "d48cba3c_38a4eacc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 56,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 56,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "16c7aba9b698e8c7cc1f5cae812d27fdf4ac1f14",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "107b4051_5b6f5e5f",
        "filename": "bluetooth/ranging/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/ranging/IBluetoothChannelSounding.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1322510
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-01T16:27:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the app can use SetMinimumSecurityLevel to select the security level.\nHowever, I believe that the app/stack should also be able to know the maximum value for the HAL (ranging algorithm).\nIf an app sets the minimum security level to 4 and both the local and remote controllers support level 4,\nthen we can enable channel sounding at level 4. \nHowever, if the ranging algorithm can only handle data for level 1, the app will get raning result with level 1 even it SetMinimumSecurityLevel with level 4",
      "parentUuid": "c718ac92_7f4fe7ef",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 56,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 56,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "16c7aba9b698e8c7cc1f5cae812d27fdf4ac1f14",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
